## 5. Functional requirements by widget

### 5.1 Inbox widget

| Interaction | Required result | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| Tap widget title/header | Open Inbox | Open Home/Today, never error page |
| Tap `Open Inbox` | Open Inbox | Open Home/Today |
| Tap task title | Open valid task detail | Open Inbox and show unavailable message if task is gone |
| Tap task checkbox | Complete task once and refresh all widgets | Open app to task only if action cannot safely finish |
| Tap quick add | Open focused Quick Add composer | Open Home then Quick Add, if available |

### 5.2 Today widget

- Header opens Today.
- Task tap opens task detail.
- Complete action toggles only from incomplete to complete for that action event; it must not toggle back because the event is delivered twice.
- If there are no current tasks, render the designed empty state and keep the header action functional.

### 5.3 Focus widget

- Focus task opens its valid detail route.
- Complete action marks the selected task complete exactly once.
- If the task was deleted, open Focus or Today and refresh. Do not retain a dead task route.

### 5.4 Quick Add widget

- Opens the Quick Add composer with autofocus only after the app reaches a stable route.
- If the composer cannot be opened because the app is restoring, open Home and display the normal add affordance; retrying must not crash or show a route error.

