## 7. Data and refresh reliability

### 7.1 Local snapshot requirement

Widgets must read a compact, versioned local snapshot rather than directly depending on a live Flutter database connection at render time.

The snapshot includes only fields required for display and actions:

- schema version
- generated timestamp
- widget instance configuration key
- task ID
- sanitized display title
- due/status flags
- completion state
- ordering index
- optional accent/theme token

Do not store raw exception details, private notes, attachments, authentication data, or any unrelated task fields in widget storage.

### 7.2 Atomic write rule

A widget update must be all-or-nothing:

1. Build and validate the full new snapshot in memory.
2. Write it to a temporary/versioned key or file.
3. Mark it current only after validation succeeds.
4. Notify the native widget provider to refresh.

If snapshot creation fails, retain the most recent valid snapshot. Do not replace working content with blank content, JSON fragments, placeholder text, or an error.

### 7.3 Refresh triggers

Refresh all relevant widget instances after:

- task add, edit, complete, reopen, delete, archive, restore
- task due-date/time or recurrence change
- list/project or focus assignment change
- selected accent/theme or widget configuration change
- application startup after local database ready
- migration completion
- timezone/date rollover
- explicit user widget refresh, where platform supports it
- package upgrade/reinstall recovery

Refresh work must be debounced for burst changes, but the final display must reflect the last successful local transaction.

### 7.4 Loading, unavailable, and empty states

| Condition | What user sees | Available action |
|---|---|---|
| First render; no snapshot yet | Branded, compact “Getting your tasks ready” state for a short time only | Tap opens Home/Today |
| No matching tasks | Intentional empty state, e.g. “Inbox is clear” | Open Inbox / Add task |
| Data migration in progress | Last valid snapshot; otherwise calm “Open Orbit to finish setup” state | Open Home |
| Snapshot corrupted/unreadable | Last valid backup snapshot; otherwise generic empty-like recovery state | Open Home |
| Task no longer exists | List refreshes; no dead row | Open relevant list |
| Platform update delay | Last valid content; no spinner that remains indefinitely | Tap opens relevant destination |

No state may contain “error,” an exception class, URI, stack trace, generic “Page Not Found,” or a blank content frame.

