## 9. Development logging and diagnostics

### 9.1 Purpose

Logging must let developers identify an exact failure stage—action creation, delivery, validation, route mapping, database operation, snapshot write, or widget render—without exposing user task content or personal data.

### 9.2 Required structured events

| Event | Required fields |
|---|---|
| `widget_render_requested` | widget type, size class, instance ID hash, snapshot version |
| `widget_render_succeeded` | widget type, duration ms, item count, used-last-good flag |
| `widget_render_failed` | widget type, stage, error category, fallback used |
| `widget_action_received` | action name, source, app state, event ID hash |
| `widget_action_validated` | action name, result, rejection reason if any |
| `widget_navigation_resolved` | action name, logical destination, internal route category |
| `widget_navigation_fallback` | source action, reason category, safe destination |
| `widget_task_action_succeeded` | action name, duration ms, refresh queued |
| `widget_task_action_rejected` | action name, reason category |
| `widget_snapshot_written` | schema version, instance count, duration ms |
| `widget_snapshot_retained` | reason category, last-good age bucket |
| `widget_refresh_requested` | widget types, trigger category |
| `widget_refresh_completed` | widget types, duration ms |

### 9.3 Privacy rules for logs

Never log:

- task title, description, notes, labels, or calendar content
- full task ID, account ID, device identifier, or raw deep link query values
- notification text or exact location data

Use route categories, hashed short-lived identifiers where needed, counts, durations, and reason codes. Verbose logs may be enabled only in debug/developer builds and must be disabled by default in production.

### 9.4 Developer debug panel

Provide an internal debug-only Widget Diagnostics screen or developer menu with:

- last snapshot generation time and schema version
- number/type of installed widget instances
- last render/refresh result per widget type
- latest sanitized action and navigation result
- a **Refresh all widgets** test control
- a **Simulate cold-start widget action** control for each supported action
- a copy/export option for sanitized diagnostics

This screen must not be included or reachable in a standard production user build.

