## 10. Regression protection

### 10.1 Isolation requirements

Widget reliability work must be isolated from unrelated working functionality.

- Do not change task schema unless a migration is required and tested.
- Do not replace the main router just to support widget links.
- Do not alter existing normal in-app route strings or page hierarchy without a migration plan.
- Do not move task write logic into widget UI code.
- Gate the new widget dispatch path behind automated tests before enabling it for existing widget instances.
- Keep a compatibility handler for widget payloads created by the immediately previous released app version.

### 10.2 Safe rollout sequence

1. Add logs and tests around current widget action failures.
2. Implement the centralized action resolver without changing visual widget layouts.
3. Add URI normalization/command mapping and unknown-route fallback.
4. Introduce versioned, atomic snapshots and refresh handling.
5. Test fresh install, update, and existing-widget compatibility.
6. Enable widget actions for internal testing.
7. Run full app regression suite.
8. Release gradually; monitor sanitized navigation-fallback and render-failure rates.

A visual redesign must be a separate change after functional reliability is proven.

