## 11. Test plan and release gates

### 11.1 Automated tests

#### Unit tests

- Each valid action payload maps to exactly one allowlisted product intent.
- `orbit://app/inbox`, `orbit://app/today`, `orbit://app/task/<valid-id>` normalize correctly.
- `orbit://inbox/`, malformed URIs, missing route pieces, unsupported schemes, and invalid task IDs never reach the router as raw strings.
- Every unsupported action returns the safe Home/Today intent.
- Completion action replay produces one state transition only.
- Missing/deleted task returns safe fallback and schedules refresh.
- Snapshot validation rejects incomplete/invalid data and retains the last known-good snapshot.

#### Widget/integration tests

- Tap each interactive region of every supported widget type.
- Verify intended screen after cold start, warm resume, and foreground action.
- Verify an Inbox action never exposes `Page Not Found` or `GoException`.
- Verify add/edit/complete/delete triggers correct widget snapshot refresh.
- Verify older payload version remains safely handled after update.
- Verify back navigation from a widget-opened destination follows the existing app rules.

### 11.2 Manual device matrix

Test on at least:

- a low/mid-range Android device and a recent flagship Android device
- Android versions supported by the app, including the oldest supported version
- at least two common launchers plus a manufacturer launcher when available
- light and dark modes
- all five Orbit accent colors
- a device after reboot, a device with app force-stopped, and a device with battery optimization enabled
- an iOS device/simulator for parity where iOS widgets are shipped

### 11.3 Mandatory scenario checklist

| Scenario | Expected result |
|---|---|
| Tap Inbox header shown in supplied screenshot | Inbox opens; no error screen |
| Tap Inbox task after task was deleted | Inbox opens/refreshes; concise unavailable message if needed |
| Tap task completion twice quickly | Task completes once; widget refreshes |
| Tap widget from cold app start | Correct destination opens after initialization |
| Tap widget while app is already open elsewhere | Correct destination replaces/navigates safely without duplicate pages |
| Launch from an old widget after app update | Valid destination or safe Home fallback |
| Database migration during widget tap | No crash/error page; safe queue/fallback |
| Corrupted widget snapshot | Last-good or recovery state; app remains usable |
| No tasks in Inbox | Purposeful “Inbox is clear” state and working Open/Add action |
| Unknown URI/action | Home/Today opens; sanitized fallback log recorded |

### 11.4 Release acceptance criteria

The release is approved only when all conditions are met:

- [ ] No supported widget path can produce `GoException`, `Page Not Found`, raw URI text, or a blank broken screen.
- [ ] 100% of automated widget action tests pass.
- [ ] All mandatory manual scenarios pass on the defined device matrix.
- [ ] Existing app navigation and task CRUD regression suite passes.
- [ ] Each widget action works from cold, warm, and foreground app states.
- [ ] Widget completion is duplicate-safe.
- [ ] Widget snapshot writes are atomic and recover to last-known-good data.
- [ ] Sanitized logs identify route mapping and fallback reasons.
- [ ] No sensitive task content appears in diagnostics.
- [ ] Product/design review confirms recovery states are calm and human-readable.

